# public_html/api/lib/ — internal includes only. No direct HTTP access.
#
# This costs the endpoint nothing. contact.php loads these files from the
# filesystem with `require __DIR__ . '/lib/...'`, and .htaccess governs HTTP
# requests, not PHP's include path — the two never meet. What it removes is the
# library's presence on the web surface.
#
# Defence in depth, not the only defence: each file here also refuses to run
# unless contact.php has defined ZONEARY_CONTACT, and answers a direct request
# with 404 and an empty body. This denies the request earlier, before PHP is
# invoked at all.
#
# Written for Apache 2.4 semantics, which is what Hostinger's LiteSpeed
# implements. Deliberately unconditional rather than wrapped in <IfModule
# mod_authz_core.c>: LiteSpeed does not report every Apache module, so a guarded
# block risks silently matching nothing and permitting access. If a server ever
# did reject this directive, direct requests to this directory would error
# rather than succeed — still a denial, and still not a path to these files.
Require all denied
